 "notes": "The whole-server replay has no villages.dat, so villagers.c makes the village collection optional in updateAITick (Java's addVillagerPosition on a real collection is list work invisible to the rows). The dev summon and structure-block villager paths set the profession the same way. lane/idxentity: EntityVillager.allowLeashing (and EntityAmbientCreature's, the bat's) answer false; ent-water-s1 right-clicks a villager with a lead and the merchant screen opens. lane/villagetrade 2026-09-27: the tail-only evidence (X-01/X-02) now points at the full re-records trade-full-s1, persist-village-full-s42, whose native replay starts before the behaviour. lane/villagetrade 2026-09-27: the !isTrading() gate on timeUntilReset is ported (H-01; trade-full-s1 failed at row 123 without it: the restock added an offer and the regeneration while the window was open); trade-prof-s1 trades one villager per profession to a lock and its unlock roll (H-02); village-life-s42 breeds three children (H-03)."
